  "rationale": "All three outputs are honest about the evidence, catch the main direct-manipulation defects and define a reduced-motion path. A wins on velocity and on rendering discipline. It specifies release velocity in px/s with a concrete clamped projection and passes the measured velocity into the settle. Its re-grab samples both the displayed position and the velocity. It is also the only output that explicitly handles conflicting transform ownership. C comes a close second, with strong interruption and snap-hysteresis detail, but it gives no units and ranks five findings as P0. B is thinner on velocity handoff and units.",
