        "velocity_projection": 14
      },
      "score": 97,
      "summary": "A labels its evidence carefully throughout. It covers input lockout, pointer-ID ownership, pointer capture, cancellation, the grab offset and 1:1 tracking. On interruption, it samples both the displayed position and the velocity. It measures velocity in CSS px/s, gives a clamped projection formula, and passes velocity into a critically damped settle. It is the only output that explicitly handles conflicting transforms by composing them or using separate wrappers. Its Reduced Motion path is strong and includes a handle-only preview. One small weakness: it hedges on whether to adopt momentum-based targeting."
    },
    "emil": {
      "blind_label": "C",
      "criteria": {
