        "direct_manipulation": 15,
        "evidence_honesty": 15,
        "interruption": 15,
        "motion_necessity": 9,
        "performance": 9,
        "velocity_projection": 13
      },
      "score": 95,
      "summary": "C's labels clearly separate Evidence, Risk and Recommendation. Its ownership and coordinate analysis is thorough, and it covers lostpointercapture and touch-action. Interruption is continuous, with velocity retargeting and a guard against stale callbacks. Velocity uses a timestamped history, accounts for a pause before release, and adds a projected endpoint and hysteresis, but gives no units. It catches the offsetTop layout reads but does not discuss conflicting transform ownership. Marking five findings P0 weakens its prioritization a little."
    }
